WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:06.250
Obviously Einsteinium has a slight resonance
for me because many

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:11.589
people think that I look like Einstein, though
of course Einstein, when he

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:13.849
was young, looked nothing like me.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:18.310
Einsteinium, the first time that was discovered
was actually in the debris

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.380
of a nuclear bomb, which has then prompted
people to make it in a

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.830
more rational and less destructive method
ever since.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.770
As far as I know that, einsteinium has absolutely
nothing to do with

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.640
Einstein, it just that people suddenly decided
that they would name

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:42.180
elements after famous scientists because they,
they had run out of

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.690
names of America and places like that.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.150
I seem to remember at GCSE-level, I don’t
even think the F elements

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.800
are even on the periodic table. I think they
are at A-level onwards. But

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.850
you don’t really cover them; they’re just
this exotic bunch of crazy

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.489
elements that do bizarre things, really interesting
bizarre things. But you

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:08.140
really don’t come into contact with them
for a long time in your career

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:12.220
and it’s only when you get past a certain
point say if you’ve already got

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.630
a PhD and you’re on doing a post-doc or
you’re an actual academic and

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:19.460
you get into research groups who handle these
types of elements on a

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.069
routine basis.

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:26.049
I still get people in the streets shouting
‘hello Einstein’ at me when they

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:27.659
are suitably drunk.

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:31.579
Why do they do that, what aspect do you think
is Einsteinesque?

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:36.079
I’m not sure though I have started the habit
of sticking out my tongue at

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:41.279
people but not in the street. I think it’s
the funny hair and the glasses,

00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:44.769
and the fact that I look like what they think
scientists ought to look like.

